First Author: Yim
Title: Bridging machine learning and clinical practice: a multicentre nomogram for 90-day graft failure risk stratification in heart transplantation
Source number: 74

Very short summary: This retrospective multicentre study used 25,200 adult heart transplant recipients from the US UNOS registry for model development and 563 recipients from Wuhan Union Hospital, China, for geographic external validation. XGBoost and Random Forest were used for predictor discovery, and the eight most influential XGBoost/SHAP predictors were translated into a logistic-regression nomogram; the final nomogram achieved an external-validation AUC of 0.671 (95% CI 0.6025–0.7386), with reported calibration and clinical net benefit.

