	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: XGBoost and Random Forest were developed from 32 pretransplant donor-recipient variables and compared with the IMPACT score. Five-fold cross-validation was used for hyperparameter optimisation. Global SHAP importance automatically selected the eight highest-impact predictors: previous cardiac surgery, recipient age, recipient bilirubin, recipient BMI, donor age, donor sex, donor BMI, and cold ischaemia time. These ML-selected variables were translated into an interpretable logistic-regression nomogram and externally validated in China. SHAP summary plots, force plots, clustering, and the nomogram provided global and patient-level interpretability.

