	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The target outcome was graft failure within 90 days after heart transplantation; the exact operational definition was deferred to the online supplemental methods and was not stated in the main article. Performance was extracted for the final eight-variable nomogram in the independent WHUH external-validation cohort: AUC 0.671 (95% CI 0.6025–0.7386). Accuracy, PPV, sensitivity, specificity, NPV, and F1-score were not reported. Calibration was assessed and the nomogram had a reported Brier score of 0.0472 in development. DCA in the external cohort showed net benefit over treat-all and treat-none strategies across risk thresholds from 0.0 to 0.4.

